scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: star-trek-tng
run_id: 2
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 18
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 48.6
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA specified tests for 'Silent error prevention (invalid TOML, bad env
    vars must error, not default)' in config_tests.rs, and config_tests.rs covers
    validation scenarios. However, the specific from_file_or_default swallowing all
    errors pattern is not explicitly called out.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified HTTP status mapping and exit codes but did not flag
    that CliError Display leaks internal details via eprintln! or that Io(transparent)
    forwards OS error details to stderr (CWE-209).
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'validate_tenant_id() exists but is never\
    \ called \u2014 at client.rs:51. A malicious tenant ID can be passed to the constructor\
    \ without validation.' TEA also wrote header injection tests. However, neither\
    \ explicitly flagged that tenant_id uses raw String instead of axiathon-core's\
    \ TenantId type."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but not the workspace
    inheritance pattern issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on ClientConfig, and Reviewer\
    \ verified: '[VERIFIED] serde(deny_unknown_fields) on ClientConfig \u2014 config\
    \ with unknown fields (including token) is rejected at config.rs:11'. TEA also\
    \ specified 'Config token rejection' tests."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. The tests were written by TEA and passed in GREEN but the
    logical flaw was not caught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. Despite SOUL.md principle 4 ('A vacuously true test is worse
    than no test'), this was not caught.
